    <item>
      <title>Advanced Solutions for Handling Corrosive Chemicals with Lined Pumps</title>
      <link>https://mis3085.github.io/docs-assoma/en/products/lining-pump/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      
      <guid>https://mis3085.github.io/docs-assoma/en/products/lining-pump/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h2 class=&#34;relative group&#34;&gt;Engineered Protection: Lined Pumps for Corrosive and Hazardous Chemicals 
    &lt;div id=&#34;engineered-protection-lined-pumps-for-corrosive-and-hazardous-chemicals&#34; class=&#34;anchor&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
    
    &lt;span
        class=&#34;absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 ltr:-left-6 rtl:-right-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100&#34;&gt;
        &lt;a class=&#34;group-hover:text-primary-300 dark:group-hover:text-neutral-700 !no-underline&#34; href=&#34;#engineered-protection-lined-pumps-for-corrosive-and-hazardous-chemicals&#34; aria-label=&#34;Anchor&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;
    &lt;/span&gt;        
    
&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lined pumps are specifically designed to address the challenges of transferring highly aggressive and corrosive chemicals. By combining an external metallic armor with a lining of advanced fluorinated engineering plastics, these pumps deliver both structural strength and exceptional chemical resistance. The magnetic drive, seal-less construction further ensures leak-free operation, making them ideal for industries where safety and reliability are paramount.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
      
    </item>
    
